 "notes": "Metrics are from greedy evaluation on the 2,000 held-out programs (seed 12345) at the final step (1000), mean \u00b1 std over seeds 0-2; the verdict uses the mean. Untested hack rate = share of uncovered branches where the greedy action is DELETE or STUB. Final FS 0.1453 is just under the 0.15 kill line (per seed 0.1435, 0.1510, 0.1415); the executor deletes covered and uncovered branches at the same rate, i.e. it never uses the message. Executor is SFT'd on the demonstrator with a uniform random message (1000 steps, batch 256, lr 2e-3); planner is a fresh MLP whose small output init makes it near-uniform. Each GRPO step samples G=8 (message, action) pairs per branch; the trajectory log-prob sums log p(m) + log p(a|m) over branches and both nets get the same group-normalised advantage. Exact KL(executor || frozen SFT executor), coef 0.02, is evaluated at the sampled messages and averaged over the G samples. Evaluation uses the greedy message and greedy action. Message accuracy = accuracy of the best of the 4 maps from symbol to covered, over all eval branches."
